00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:49.680
Fast fact number three is also a belated fast fact.

176
00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:54.400
I realized I missed something a couple of episodes back in the fight.

177
00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:54.840
What?

178
00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:59.300
Which applies to all the episodes moving forward, talking about cold opens.

179
00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:00.220
Oh.

180
00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:03.200
Do you want to tell folks what a cold open is?

181
00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:03.600
Yes.

182
00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:09.760
So in a script, scripts usually have like a three-act structure where you tell the story,

183
00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:10.760
right?

184
00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:12.400
And like a little mini three-act.

185
00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:12.700
Yeah.

186
00:07:13.180 --> 00:07:17.560
Well, we started doing this thing that we called the cold open, and it's before the credits,

187
00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:23.320
and it's a little joke or almost like a standalone moment that might apply later to the episode,

188
00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:24.280
but also might not.

189
00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:24.640
Might not.

190
00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:26.420
It's just like its own little moment.

191
00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:28.180
So that was something that our show did.

192
00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:32.460
We had these little cold opens, and then we're also going to start adding tags soon.

193
00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:33.500
Ooh, tags are fun.

194
00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:34.560
Tags were-

195
00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:35.540
At the end.

196
00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:36.280
At the very end.

197
00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:39.980
We would come back from a commercial break, and you'd get like a seven-second tag.

198
00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:40.860
They were very short.

199
00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:41.620
Really short.

200
00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:42.560
Another little joke.

201
00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:46.620
Yeah, they were always really short, like maybe just one page, three lines, just something

202
00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:47.220
really tiny.

203
00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:47.780
Yes.

204
00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:55.000
In this episode, we have a cold open that is one of our most famous cold opens, the Fitness

205
00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:55.600
Orb.

206
00:07:55.820 --> 00:07:56.300
Yes.

207
00:07:56.560 --> 00:08:00.740
Which is so great, and we had a ton of fan questions about this.

208
00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:03.460
It's probably our most frequently asked moment.

209
00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:05.360
About this episode, for sure.

210
00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:05.920
Definitely.

211
00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:13.540
For example, Fernanda Fuentes and Derek Ford both asked, how many times did you have to

212
00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:16.180
film the cold open with Dwight's fitness ball?

213
00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:21.480
And David Nicholas asked, how many fitness orbs did you go through before it popped just

214
00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:21.840
right?

215
00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:25.180
Well, everyone, it was not meant to pop.

216
00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:28.980
Oh, Jenna, Jenna, you look really excited.

217
00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:30.500
Are you sitting on some info?

218
00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:32.120
I'm sitting on some info.

219
00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:34.820
I traded messages with Phil Shea.

220
00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:36.620
Phil Shea, prop master.

221
00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:37.520
Yes.

222
00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:40.660
He told me all about the fitness orbs.

223
00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:43.580
So first of all, he bought 17.

224
00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:45.740
17 fitness orbs.

225
00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:46.140
Yes.

226
00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:48.920
And he practiced with John using three of them.

227
00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:52.560
Phil Shea sat on them, and John like hit them.

228
00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:55.980
Phil Shea was such, talk about a trooper, Phil Shea.

229
00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:56.740
He's amazing.

230
00:08:57.060 --> 00:09:01.840
So the idea was that John would stick the scissors into the fitness orb, and it would

231
00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:03.240
deflate very slowly.

232
00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:08.620
And the camera would be in front of Dwight's desk, and you would just see him very slowly

233
00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:12.500
melt to the floor as Jim very smugly.

234
00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:13.400
Looks on.

235
00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:13.860
Yes.

236
00:09:14.060 --> 00:09:15.660
That was what was in the script.

237
00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:19.180
So they practiced three times.

238
00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:20.320
It worked perfectly.

239
00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:23.200
And they had 14 left for the scene.

240
00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:28.420
And Phil said to John, as long as you don't hit the seam of the ball with the scissors, which

241
00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:32.740
would be like a one in a million chance that you could do it, the ball will slowly deflate,

242
00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:34.100
and it will work as planned.

243
00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:36.640
It's also very hard to see the seam.

244
00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:37.520
Oh, yeah.

245
00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:37.820
Yeah.

246
00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:39.600
I mean, yeah.

247
00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:41.160
You would have to hit it just right.

248
00:09:41.420 --> 00:09:41.800
Yes.

249
00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:43.960
It would be basically impossible to do.

250
00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:49.880
So they did 13 takes, and it worked just right, and everyone was happy, and they were

251
00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:50.860
about to move on.

252
00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:54.120
And Phil said, I have one more ball.

253
00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:54.680
Yeah.

254
00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:57.300
So Paul Feig said, oh, what the heck?

255
00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:58.260
Let's just do one more.

256
00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:03.080
And in all the 13 takes, you guys, Rain, as Dwight, slowly sunk to the ground.

257
00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:03.980
Like, phew.

258
00:10:04.220 --> 00:10:04.380
Yeah.

259
00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:04.840
Right?

260
00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:05.600
And it was perfect.

261
00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:09.160
So they have an extra ball.

