356
00:13:57.710 --> 00:13:58.550
It's good, guys.

357
00:13:58.550 --> 00:13:59.470
It's going to be good.

358
00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:02.170
And Greg, you know, as you guys know, so brilliant.

359
00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:06.150
I feel Greg's philosophy was just write it as if we're going to go off the air, you

360
00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:09.730
know, so we don't write ourselves in the corner, especially with Pam and Jim and all

361
00:14:09.730 --> 00:14:15.340
that kind of stuff, and just, you know, just have as much fun as feeling in the writer's

362
00:14:15.340 --> 00:14:19.280
room that we might be off the air.

363
00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:20.380
I mean, we'll just go for it.

