00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:23.320
That's such a good insight, because I felt that way, too.

365
00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:27.960
I felt like we were making the show in a bubble or making it for our own amusement sometimes.

366
00:14:28.480 --> 00:14:30.640
Do you remember our table reads in the beginning?

367
00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:31.680
They weren't around a table.

368
00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:33.140
We would just sit on the set.

369
00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:36.240
We'd all pull up our desk chairs, and we'd sit in a circle.

370
00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:40.460
And then during our hiatus, I did a guest star, and I went in for the table read, and

371
00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:41.960
it was like a big deal.

372
00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:46.980
There was a big table, and everyone sat around it, and you had like a little placard with

373
00:14:46.980 --> 00:14:52.360
