I know.

1034
00:41:26.740 --> 00:41:30.840
Do you remember on the day, we rehearsed that scene because it was a little tricky.

1035
00:41:30.840 --> 00:41:35.520
There was a big camera movement of Michael watching the door, waiting for Jan, and then

1036
00:41:35.520 --> 00:41:36.580
he comes out of his office.

1037
00:41:37.260 --> 00:41:38.260
So it was a little complicated.

1038
00:41:38.260 --> 00:41:39.980
We had to really rehearse that with the cameras.

1039
00:41:40.340 --> 00:41:43.980
And during the rehearsal, Steve accidentally…

1040
00:41:43.980 --> 00:41:45.080
Touched her boob.

1041
00:41:45.180 --> 00:41:45.500
Yes.

1042
00:41:45.660 --> 00:41:47.420
And we all laughed so hard.

1043
00:41:47.560 --> 00:41:48.820
Melora was cracking up.

1044
00:41:48.960 --> 00:41:51.260
Melora said, you have to do that in a take.

1045
00:41:51.360 --> 00:41:52.360
And Steve was like, no, no, no.

1046
00:41:52.420 --> 00:41:54.700
And she's like, no, it was so funny and awkward.

1047
00:41:54.700 --> 00:41:55.400
You have to.

1048
00:41:55.400 --> 00:41:58.280
And so then that became a bit in the scene.

1049
00:41:58.460 --> 00:42:02.200
Then they had to try to do it where it still looked like an accident, which is a really

1050
00:42:02.200 --> 00:42:03.300
hard thing to do, actually.

1051
00:42:03.460 --> 00:42:04.320
Yeah, because he was just…

1052
00:42:04.320 --> 00:42:04.940
To recreate that.

1053
00:42:05.080 --> 00:42:07.600
I think Steve was just trying to pat her shoulder and missed.

1054
00:42:07.940 --> 00:42:08.300
Yes.

1055
00:42:08.300 --> 00:42:08.560
Yes.

1056
00:42:08.780 --> 00:42:11.540
She sort of moved a little bit and he accidentally patted her boob.

1057
00:42:11.540 --> 00:42:11.660
Yeah.

1058
00:42:11.660 --> 00:42:14.080
She turned into him as he went to pat her shoulder.

1059
00:42:14.560 --> 00:42:15.280
So funny.

1060
00:42:15.500 --> 00:42:15.920
So funny.

1061
00:42:25.400 --> 00:42:30.060
I love that the cameras are outside of the office during this scene between Michael and

1062
00:42:30.060 --> 00:42:30.280
Jan.

1063
00:42:30.580 --> 00:42:34.180
So Paul Feig talked about his decision to keep the cameras outside the office for these

1064
00:42:34.180 --> 00:42:34.560
scenes.

1065
00:42:34.800 --> 00:42:41.820
He thought that Michael might want Jan alone so that he could ask her about the relationship.

1066
00:42:42.020 --> 00:42:43.320
And so the camera…

1067
00:42:43.320 --> 00:42:45.580
And Jan would not want the cameras there anyway.

1068
00:42:45.760 --> 00:42:46.820
No, probably not.

1069
00:42:46.820 --> 00:42:48.880
And so they had to get it as a spy shot.

1070
00:42:49.020 --> 00:42:54.380
But then later, after the suggestion box meeting, you'll notice that the camera is inside the

1071
00:42:54.380 --> 00:42:55.020
room with them.

1072
00:42:55.280 --> 00:43:01.280
And Paul said that his logic was that in Michael's mind, if he let the cameras in the office

1073
00:43:01.280 --> 00:43:05.660
with him, maybe Jan couldn't yell at him as much for what happened in the conference

1074
00:43:05.660 --> 00:43:05.960
room.

1075
00:43:06.060 --> 00:43:06.680
Oh, yes.

1076
00:43:06.680 --> 00:43:09.240
So Michael would be able to use the camera as a buffer.

1077
00:43:09.380 --> 00:43:10.000
As protection.

1078
00:43:10.280 --> 00:43:15.360
I just love the thoughtfulness that goes into the planning of where the camera is or where

1079
00:43:15.360 --> 00:43:16.300
the camera isn't.

1080
00:43:17.220 --> 00:43:18.500
I mean, that's just…

1081
00:43:18.500 --> 00:43:19.340
Paul is so smart.

1082
00:43:19.520 --> 00:43:20.440
He's so smart.

1083
00:43:20.440 --> 00:43:26.040
Well, I loved the line that Jan had when she said, please don't smell me, Michael.

1084
00:43:26.760 --> 00:43:27.480
Oh, yes.

1085
00:43:28.260 --> 00:43:29.260
He's like, what are you wearing?

1086
00:43:29.340 --> 00:43:30.260
It smells sexy.

1087
00:43:30.340 --> 00:43:31.860
She's like, oh, God, don't smell me.

1088
00:43:31.860 --> 00:43:32.380
Please don't smell me, Michael.

1089
00:43:32.500 --> 00:43:35.480
That reminds me so much of Pam's line, please don't throw garbage at me.

1090
00:43:35.580 --> 00:43:36.000
Me too.

1091
00:43:36.020 --> 00:43:37.500
It reminded me of the same thing.

1092
00:43:37.680 --> 00:43:40.060
Hey, guys, just a little fun background thing to catch.

1093
00:43:40.180 --> 00:43:42.500
There is a British flag on Michael's desk.

1094
00:43:42.720 --> 00:43:45.540
You see it throughout the episode whenever you go into his office.

1095
00:43:45.880 --> 00:43:48.680
I like to think it's a little nod to our BBC roots.

1096
00:43:48.980 --> 00:43:49.680
It must be.

1097
00:43:49.680 --> 00:43:50.120
Right?

1098
00:43:50.340 --> 00:43:50.980
I think so.

1099
00:43:51.080 --> 00:43:51.240
Yeah.

1100
00:43:51.540 --> 00:43:52.520
They would do stuff like that.

1101
00:43:52.600 --> 00:43:52.900
I know.

1102
00:43:53.020 --> 00:43:55.200
So I don't know if you guys noticed it, but I noticed it right away.

1103
00:43:55.360 --> 00:44:00.780
In the conference room, 12 minutes, 26 seconds, we are opening up the suggestion box.

1104
00:44:00.940 --> 00:44:03.220
We had a fan question from RealBrandonB16.

1105
00:44:03.680 --> 00:44:06.380
What was the hardest scene for you to film for this episode?

1106
00:44:06.780 --> 00:44:07.460
This one.

1107
00:44:07.760 --> 00:44:09.960
We laughed so much.

1108
00:44:10.420 --> 00:44:11.220
So hard.

1109
00:44:11.320 --> 00:44:14.380
I laughed so hard at every one of Steve's reactions.

1110
00:44:14.920 --> 00:44:15.780
Everything was so…

1111
00:44:15.780 --> 00:44:20.100
And also, like, Rain is Dwight, like, repeating all the ridiculous things.

1112
00:44:20.300 --> 00:44:21.040
So good.

1113
00:44:21.460 --> 00:44:24.840
Also, I think in this scene there's some Toby sass.

1114
00:44:25.020 --> 00:44:25.880
Oh, I wrote.

1115
00:44:25.940 --> 00:44:26.460
Did you spot?

1116
00:44:26.460 --> 00:44:27.860
Major Toby sass.

1117
00:44:28.420 --> 00:44:28.860
Okay.

1118
00:44:28.940 --> 00:44:29.220
So wait.

1119
00:44:29.220 --> 00:44:34.420
First of all, can we just briefly talk about how many cards are in the suggestion box?

1120
00:44:34.500 --> 00:44:34.980
Yes, please.

1121
00:44:35.280 --> 00:44:36.140
There are six.

1122
00:44:36.360 --> 00:44:36.580
Okay.

1123
00:44:36.840 --> 00:44:39.720
Number one, what should we do to prepare for Y2K?

1124
00:44:40.340 --> 00:44:40.780
Amazing.

1125
00:44:41.360 --> 00:44:45.880
Number two, we need better outreach for employees fighting depression.

1126
00:44:46.280 --> 00:44:46.460
Okay.

1127
00:44:46.720 --> 00:44:47.360
That was Tom.

1128
00:44:47.940 --> 00:44:50.880
Number three, you need to do something about your BO.

1129
00:44:51.540 --> 00:44:53.900
This is when we have major Toby sass.

1130
00:44:54.060 --> 00:44:54.420
Yes.

1131
00:44:54.640 --> 00:44:56.400
Because he's like, Michael, aren't these about you?

1132
00:44:56.520 --> 00:44:59.880
And he's like, I mean, I can't believe Toby – first of all, I can't believe Michael

1133
00:44:59.880 --> 00:45:01.520
didn't kick him out of the conference room.

1134
00:45:01.580 --> 00:45:01.700
Yeah.

1135
00:45:01.700 --> 00:45:01.780
Yeah.

1136
00:45:02.160 --> 00:45:02.480
Right?

1137
00:45:02.800 --> 00:45:05.200
I think he only didn't kick him out because Jan was there.

1138
00:45:05.340 --> 00:45:05.760
Yes.

1139
00:45:05.860 --> 00:45:06.340
Good call.

1140
00:45:06.340 --> 00:45:12.700
Also, can we all just take a minute to witness the fact that Creed, like, schooled Michael

1141
00:45:12.700 --> 00:45:14.920
and the difference between inferring and implying?

1142
00:45:15.180 --> 00:45:15.460
Yes.

1143
00:45:15.800 --> 00:45:16.620
Like, what, Creed?

1144
00:45:17.400 --> 00:45:20.900
I love when Creed suddenly lays down real wisdom.

1145
00:45:21.120 --> 00:45:21.420
Yeah.

1146
00:45:21.620 --> 00:45:22.380
And we're like, what?

1147
00:45:22.840 --> 00:45:23.200
Yeah.

1148
00:45:23.460 --> 00:45:26.260
He mostly says gibberish, and then you're like, oh, okay.

1149
00:45:26.260 --> 00:45:26.420
Yeah.

1150
00:45:26.580 --> 00:45:27.040
Take note.

1151
00:45:27.420 --> 00:45:29.060
Inferring and implying are two different things.

1152
00:45:29.220 --> 00:45:29.380
What?

1153
00:45:29.560 --> 00:45:34.280
Number four, you need to do something about your coffee breath, which was clearly my character's

1154
00:45:34.280 --> 00:45:34.580
card.

1155
00:45:34.820 --> 00:45:35.300
Yes.

1156
00:45:35.720 --> 00:45:36.040
Yes.

1157
00:45:36.580 --> 00:45:38.380
Number five, a piece of gum.

1158
00:45:38.580 --> 00:45:40.700
Number six, don't sleep with your boss.

1159
00:45:40.900 --> 00:45:41.420
Yes.

1160
00:45:41.680 --> 00:45:41.980
Yeah.

1161
00:45:42.460 --> 00:45:45.520
I personally never came back from the gum.

1162
00:45:45.980 --> 00:45:49.800
When he opens up the piece of gum and Steve's reaction to the gum.

1163
00:45:49.960 --> 00:45:50.200
Yeah.

1164
00:45:50.860 --> 00:45:55.320
I don't think I ever got it together after that because it was so amazing.

1165
00:45:55.920 --> 00:45:59.620
Also, watch Mindy at 15 minutes, 10 seconds.

1166
00:45:59.980 --> 00:46:04.960
She puts her hand over her mouth, but her eyes get really wide.

1167
00:46:04.960 --> 00:46:06.920
Like, she's totally – it's a total giveaway.

1168
00:46:06.940 --> 00:46:07.520
She's laughing.

1169
00:46:07.720 --> 00:46:09.040
That's what Mindy does when she laughs.

1170
00:46:09.100 --> 00:46:10.940
She covers her mouth with her hand.

1171
00:46:10.980 --> 00:46:11.240
Yes.

1172
00:46:11.420 --> 00:46:12.100
That's her tell.

1173
00:46:12.300 --> 00:46:12.560
All right.

1174
00:46:12.660 --> 00:46:17.020
So now we're going to move out to the stairwell and the scene where Dwight is pumping himself

1175
00:46:17.020 --> 00:46:18.580
up for his performance review.

1176
00:46:18.580 --> 00:46:21.600
To the song Wild Side by Motley Crue.

1177
00:46:21.800 --> 00:46:22.140
Yes.

1178
00:46:22.560 --> 00:46:26.360
So that is the stairwell to the writer's offices.

1179
00:46:26.700 --> 00:46:30.300
The bottom of the stairs is the hallway where our editors would sit.

1180
00:46:30.560 --> 00:46:31.960
That's where the editing bays were.

1181
00:46:31.960 --> 00:46:33.280
And upstairs was the writers.

1182
00:46:33.800 --> 00:46:38.460
And Rain has said in interviews that this was one of his favorite scenes to film.

1183
00:46:39.020 --> 00:46:43.800
And I happened to be over in the writer's room that day that they were filming it.

1184
00:46:43.880 --> 00:46:47.400
And I sat at the top of the stairs and I watched him film the scene.

1185
00:46:47.520 --> 00:46:47.820
Yes.

1186
00:46:48.040 --> 00:46:49.620
And it was so great.

1187
00:46:49.620 --> 00:46:53.020
And a lot of the stuff that he is saying there was improvised.

1188
00:46:53.200 --> 00:46:53.440
Yes.

1189
00:46:53.560 --> 00:46:56.880
As his – also, people were like, did he improvise playing the air guitar?

1190
00:46:57.000 --> 00:46:57.760
That's all Rain.

1191
00:46:57.920 --> 00:46:58.800
That's all Rain.

1192
00:46:58.800 --> 00:47:00.940
And there was something funny about that.

1193
00:47:01.080 --> 00:47:06.460
So usually when you have music in a scene, they don't actually play the music on set.

1194
00:47:06.700 --> 00:47:10.580
In fact, there'll be like a big dance scene or a club scene.

1195
00:47:10.720 --> 00:47:11.940
Like let's say you're shooting a wedding.

1196
00:47:12.140 --> 00:47:15.860
They'll play a few seconds of the music so that you can get the beat.

1197
00:47:15.900 --> 00:47:18.860
And then they turn it off and you have to dance.

1198
00:47:19.120 --> 00:47:19.980
With no music.

1199
00:47:20.060 --> 00:47:21.760
With no music and say your dialogue.

1200
00:47:22.020 --> 00:47:23.980
And then they add the music later in editing.

1201
00:47:23.980 --> 00:47:29.160
And that's so they can get your dialogue clean and so that they can cut between different takes.

1202
00:47:29.340 --> 00:47:31.420
And you don't want this song in the background.

1203
00:47:31.820 --> 00:47:37.600
Well, for this scene, they actually played the music on the boombox.

1204
00:47:37.900 --> 00:47:41.680
And it made for a bit of a challenge in the editing room.

1205
00:47:41.680 --> 00:47:51.720
But Greg felt like it provided so much to Rain's performance for him to have that music blaring.

1206
00:47:52.120 --> 00:47:53.760
And also, it's documentary.

1207
00:47:54.000 --> 00:47:59.720
So you wouldn't have this like clean track of the music playing later.

1208
00:47:59.940 --> 00:48:01.720
Although we did in Cafe Disco.

1209
00:48:01.920 --> 00:48:03.280
We all had to dance to nothing.

1210
00:48:03.280 --> 00:48:03.700
I remember that.

1211
00:48:03.820 --> 00:48:04.060
Yeah.

1212
00:48:04.380 --> 00:48:07.640
In the little Michael Scott paper company thing.

1213
00:48:07.640 --> 00:48:08.180
All right.

1214
00:48:08.320 --> 00:48:10.740
So now we move into Michael's office.

1215
00:48:11.000 --> 00:48:15.760
And Dwight is going to give his pitch for why he deserves a raise.

1216
00:48:16.140 --> 00:48:16.340
Okay.

1217
00:48:16.420 --> 00:48:19.240
This scene happens at around 17 minutes, 14 seconds.

1218
00:48:19.500 --> 00:48:22.760
I just have to tell you guys, I did a lot of scenes with Rainn Wilson.

1219
00:48:23.220 --> 00:48:25.500
And here's something you have to know about him.

1220
00:48:25.860 --> 00:48:27.960
The man loves a prop.

1221
00:48:28.200 --> 00:48:30.640
He loves a prop, guys.

1222
00:48:30.660 --> 00:48:31.000
He does.

1223
00:48:31.180 --> 00:48:32.040
Oh, my gosh.

1224
00:48:32.180 --> 00:48:35.120
So it was no surprise to me when he held up that binder.

1225
00:48:35.120 --> 00:48:39.520
I have a feeling him and Phil Shea talked a lot about that binder and what would go in it.

1226
00:48:39.660 --> 00:48:41.140
But Rainn loves a prop.

1227
00:48:41.440 --> 00:48:47.880
Well, you can see at 18 minutes, 12 seconds, speaking of props, there is a sign.

1228
00:48:48.140 --> 00:48:48.640
Mm-hmm.

1229
00:48:48.920 --> 00:48:52.440
And it never gets referred to in the scene because it got deleted.

1230
00:48:52.980 --> 00:48:56.820
Dwight has made a sign of himself where he breaks down his name.

1231
00:48:57.040 --> 00:48:57.960
I wrote it all down.

1232
00:48:58.000 --> 00:48:59.020
I did, too.

1233
00:48:59.220 --> 00:48:59.720
Okay, say it, Ange.

1234
00:48:59.720 --> 00:49:00.600
Let's take turns.

1235
00:49:00.760 --> 00:49:01.360
You do the first one.

1236
00:49:01.460 --> 00:49:02.340
Well, let's go back and forth.

1237
00:49:02.520 --> 00:49:02.660
Okay.

1238
00:49:02.820 --> 00:49:04.380
Dwight's acronym for his name.

1239
00:49:05.180 --> 00:49:05.720
Determined.

1240
00:49:05.960 --> 00:49:06.600
Worker.

1241
00:49:07.320 --> 00:49:08.020
Intense.

1242
00:49:08.580 --> 00:49:09.600
Good worker.

1243
00:49:10.000 --> 00:49:10.820
Hard worker.

1244
00:49:11.080 --> 00:49:11.620
Terrific.

1245
00:49:13.320 --> 00:49:19.560
You actually, I have to advise people to go back and watch the deleted scenes from this

1246
00:49:19.560 --> 00:49:23.280
because there is a whole scene where he explains this.

1247
00:49:24.080 --> 00:49:27.080
First, he explains it to Jim at their desks.

1248
00:49:27.240 --> 00:49:32.540
And then he makes suggestions for what Jim's acronym could be.

1249
00:49:33.090 --> 00:49:33.700
He does?

1250
00:49:33.700 --> 00:49:35.160
Yes, and it's really good.

1251
00:49:35.340 --> 00:49:39.840
And then they also show the scene from Michael's office.

1252
00:49:39.880 --> 00:49:40.900
So it's good stuff.

1253
00:49:41.080 --> 00:49:45.900
It is interesting to me that the two characters that were the most excited about their performance

1254
00:49:45.900 --> 00:49:47.300
review were Dwight and Angela.

1255
00:49:47.900 --> 00:49:52.240
I mean, Dwight put so much effort into his, and then all Michael said was he's adequate.

1256
00:49:52.560 --> 00:49:55.540
And then my character is like, I love to be judged.

1257
00:49:55.600 --> 00:49:57.880
I think I hold up even to the most severe scrutiny.

1258
00:49:58.040 --> 00:49:59.240
I'm so excited for this.

1259
00:49:59.240 --> 00:50:02.100
And then he just slams the door in my face and says, you're satisfactory.

1260
00:50:02.660 --> 00:50:03.480
Oh, I know.

1261
00:50:03.580 --> 00:50:04.260
It's so sad.

1262
00:50:04.260 --> 00:50:07.800
The two people who really wanted a performance review don't get it.

1263
00:50:07.960 --> 00:50:10.740
So around 18 minutes, Jan is fed up.

1264
00:50:10.900 --> 00:50:11.480
She's like, you know what?

1265
00:50:11.480 --> 00:50:12.140
I need a minute.

1266
00:50:12.300 --> 00:50:13.280
I'm going to step out.

1267
00:50:13.280 --> 00:50:14.600
I'm going to collect my thoughts.

1268
00:50:14.800 --> 00:50:18.420
And she goes into the hallway, and we see the sign for the building.

1269
00:50:18.440 --> 00:50:20.620
And here's what's in the building that we see.

1270
00:50:21.260 --> 00:50:22.980
WB Jones Heating and Air.

1271
00:50:23.480 --> 00:50:25.120
That's in Office 110.

1272
00:50:26.340 --> 00:50:27.760
Available 1,400.

1273
00:50:28.140 --> 00:50:29.620
It's available space.

1274
00:50:29.800 --> 00:50:31.240
And then the number is 120.

1275
00:50:31.540 --> 00:50:31.740
What?

1276
00:50:32.040 --> 00:50:33.740
Then we have Dunder Mifflin, Inc.

1277
00:50:34.040 --> 00:50:34.860
Suite 200.

1278
00:50:34.860 --> 00:50:37.600
And then we have Vance Refrigeration, Suite 210.

1279
00:50:38.440 --> 00:50:40.080
So here's something that's interesting.

1280
00:50:41.260 --> 00:50:46.340
We haven't done that episode where we meet all the people in the business park yet.

1281
00:50:46.620 --> 00:50:48.420
But they had to make that prop.

1282
00:50:48.960 --> 00:50:49.360
Yeah.

1283
00:50:49.680 --> 00:50:50.920
So I want to ask.

1284
00:50:51.140 --> 00:50:52.580
That would actually be set deck.

1285
00:50:52.740 --> 00:50:54.220
I want to ask Michael Gallenberg.

1286
00:50:54.400 --> 00:50:58.160
Did he just randomly make up that JB whatever?

1287
00:50:58.760 --> 00:50:59.820
The WB.

1288
00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:01.780
And did he make up Vance Refrigeration?

1289
00:51:01.800 --> 00:51:02.540
WB Jones.

